<title>USA: U.S. factory lard use - Census.</title>
<headline>U.S. factory lard use - Census.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. factories used 36.3 million lbs of lard in edible and inedible product output in June 1997 versus 39.9 million lbs in May and 31.4 million lbs in June 1996 the Census Bureau said.</p>
<p>Usage so far in the 1997 period amounted to 200.7 million lbs versus 216.8 million lbs in the 1996 period.</p>
<p>Usage includes hydrogenated vegetable and animal fats and other fats and oils in process.</p>
</text>
